Z||000000||RiceBurner515||11-09-2000||09:16 PM||||I have a coolant leak that i found where it is coming from...its coming from the side of the block (right side on 85SE). I'm not sure what its called or anything, i took out 3 bolts from the block and took off a metal piece with a circular gasket on it. There was a big "chamber" where the coolant is stored in the block, does anybody kknow what this is called and what kind of gasket do i ask for. Also, has anybody ever had a leak from here b4, im not sure if its just a loose bolt, gasket, or a crack in the block. Please respond ASAP, thanks!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bob Englert||11-09-2000||09:34 PM||||Is this in the passenger side between the alternator and the water pump in the 4 cyl?  The front of the engine block?<P>This sounds like the cover for the opening used for the water pump on other cars that used the 2.5 motor.  If this is so you should be able to find a gasket or just use some RTV to seal the cover plate.<P>This is my guess anyway!<P>Good luck....<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>87 Coupe<BR>85 SE (For Sale)||||reg||1
